If you know how to do the nurse dance, it's a good thing to do before
attempting a castle assault.  You'll need a no-teleport level (Sokoban).
Wish for 2 cursed scrolls of genocide.  If you're feeling cowardly,
use that blessed magic marker to write a few blessed scrolls of genocide,
take out L and h.  If you're feeling *really* cowardly, take out ; as
well.  Of course, you can only write ?oGeno after you've identified it,
so you'll likely have to wish for at one of these batches.  Don't wish
for both!  Note: there is no shame in feeling cowardly in assaulting
the castle for the first time.  It's really hard!

SDSM is always appropriate (unless you already have it, of course).

>From the other posts, you seem to have +Magic Missile, which is 
*highly* important for a wizard.  Don't bother with an alternative
weapon, spells are much better for a wiz.  You're high-level, so a
blessed spellbook of finger of death is an option, too, although
I'd say it's a low priority.  If you're skilled or higher in attack
spells, try a spellbook of cone of cold.  It works wonders.

Speed boots are even more important than SDSM, in my opinion.

Wish more more magic markers to write enchant armor scrolls.  AC -19
is reasonably good, but to be sure, I'd want -30 or so.

It will help a lot in the main battles if you have a ring of conflict.
Wish for a blessed one.  The monsters will mainly attack each other
instead of you.  Not totally, though.

Lifesaving is always a good option, especially when assaulting
the castle for the first time.

Overall, since you already have SDSM and have ?oCharging identified,
I'd use the following six wishes to maximize castle survival:

blessed fixed +3 speed boots
blessed magic marker (use to write 2 b?oCharging, use 1 on 
                      the wand and write bunch of ?oEA -- use the 
			second b?oCharing on the marker itself).
blessed ring of conflict
2 blessed scrolls of genocide (Lh)
blessed spellbook of cone of cold, unless you've already 
	found one.
blessed amulet of life saving

